  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0125 database is designed to manage a movie rental system, storing information about actors, films, customers, staff, and stores. The actor table contains details about individual actors, including their first and last names, and is linked to the film_actor table, which associates actors with the films they have appeared in. The film table holds information about each movie, such as its title, description, release year, and rental duration, and is connected to the film_category table, which links films to their respective categories. The film_text table stores the title and description of each film in a full-text index for efficient searching. The inventory table tracks the availability of films in each store, while the language table lists the languages in which films are available. The payment table records transactions made by customers, including the amount paid and the date of payment, and is linked to the customer and staff tables. The rental table tracks the rental history of each customer, including the date they rented a film and the date they returned it, and is connected to the inventory and staff tables. The staff table contains details about each staff member, including their first and last names, address, and username, and is linked to the address and store tables. The store table holds information about each store, including its manager and address, and is linked to the address and staff tables. The address table stores the addresses of customers, staff, and stores, while the city table contains information about each city, including its name and country, and is linked to the country table. The country table lists the countries in which stores are located.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThis project involves the Sakila test database, a fictional and simplified database designed to manage a video rental store. It contains data structures relevant to tracking movies, customers, rentals, and payments in a video rental business context.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe objective is to create a database system that efficiently manages various aspects of a video rental business, including movie information, inventory management, customer records, rental transactions, and related payments.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Store Managers: Oversee store operations and manage inventory.\n- Staff: Handle customer interactions, process rentals, and manage transactions.\n- Customers: Rent movies and interact with store services.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Movie Management:\n   - Store and manage details about films, including titles, descriptions, release years, languages, ratings, and special features.\n   - Categorize films into different genres using a category system.\n\n2. Inventory Management:\n   - Track inventory of films across different stores.\n\n3. Customer Management:\n   - Maintain records of customer details including addresses, contact information, and rental history.\n   - Manage active status of customers.\n\n4. Rental Processing:\n   - Record rental transactions including rental dates and return dates.\n   - Associate each rental with a customer and store staff member.\n\n5. Payment Processing:\n   - Process payments linked to rental transactions.\n   - Store details of payment amounts and dates.\n\n6. Staff Management:\n   - Manage staff details for operational purposes.\n   - Assign staff members to stores.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Database Integrity: Ensure referential integrity through the use of foreign keys.\n- User Access Control: Allow different levels of access for managers, staff, and customers.\n- Scalability: Support potential increase in data and user interactions.\n- Data Consistency: Maintain data accuracy with constraints and default values.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0125.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0125\nCREATE TABLE `actor` (\n  `actor_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`actor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `film` (\n  `film_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `release_year` year DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rental_duration` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`film_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `film_actor` (\n  `film_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `actor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`film_id`, `actor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `film_actor_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`film_id`) REFERENCES `film` (`film_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `film_actor_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`actor_id`) REFERENCES `actor` (`actor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `film_category` (\n  `film_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`film_id`, `category_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `film_category_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`film_id`) REFERENCES `film` (`film_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `film_text` (\n  `film_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`film_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `film_text_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`film_id`) REFERENCES `film` (`film_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `inventory` (\n  `inventory_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `film_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `store_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`inventory_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `inventory_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`film_id`) REFERENCES `film` (`film_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `language` (\n  `language_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`language_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `payment` (\n  `payment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`payment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `payment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `payment_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`staff_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`staff_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `rental` (\n  `rental_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `inventory_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rental_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `return_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`rental_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `rental_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`inventory_id`) REFERENCES `inventory` (`inventory_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `staff` (\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`staff_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `staff_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`address_id`) REFERENCES `address` (`address_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `store` (\n  `store_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `manager_staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`store_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `store_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`manager_staff_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`staff_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `store_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`address_id`) REFERENCES `address` (`address_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `address` (\n  `address_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `city_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`address_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `address_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`city_id`) REFERENCES `city` (`city_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `city` (\n  `city_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `city` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `country_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`city_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `city_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`country_id`) REFERENCES `country` (`country_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `country` (\n  `country_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `country` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`country_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
